  "term": "emulation",
  "definition": "In this historical educational sense, emulation means the desire and effort to match or outdo another person, taking the form of competitive imitation or rivalry. The source describes it as a teaching principle used to stimulate effort, while also warning that it can shift attention away from learning itself toward personal competition.",
